  ],
  reason: "WHY RUST RATHER THAN .dag: the substrate has no directory enumeration sufficient to BIND each sibling `.dag` as a typed row value. Membership discovery exists (`v2.std.decl_index` `data_decl_type_facts`); value binding does not. Until that grounding lands, a checkout carries no roster module for the importers (`gunbc.design_ledgers`, `gunbc.ledger_row_coherence`, `gunbc.rung_drop.standing` and its readers, `test.claim.generated_artifact_merge_driver_real_execution_witness`) unless the host contributes one, and the required parse join reports RosterModuleAbsent on the intended steady state. THE BOUNDARY IS SOURCE ACQUISITION, AND IT WRITES NOTHING: every walk that acquires a source population hands each directory's listing to acquire_dir_files, which returns AcquiredDag sources -- the listed files, plus for a row directory the roster rendered (render_roster) from the sibling contents that same call read -- so compiler_sources = acquired_sources + derive_rosters(acquired_sources) from one read of the rows. AcquiredDag has no Deref to Path, so a consumer cannot reach the disk for a module that has no file. A physical file at a reserved roster identity refuses, located, and is never consumed, overridden or deleted by the loader; an unreadable row refuses rather than shortening the roster. The earlier realization wrote a gitignored roster.dag into the checkout on every walk, which dirtied the checkout each invocation admitted and made deploy candidate admission refuse; that writer (ensure_if_row_dir, ensure_if_row_dir_or_panic, ensure_derived_roster, write_atomically, row_stems) is DELETED, and the deploy-scope exemption it forced is deleted with it. That is a section 7 seed realization of a missing capability, not a scaffold: dissolution is grounded in gunbc.guarantee_stall.roster_re_enumerates_its_own_rows_stall (declaration-value binding), not in a sentence in the Rust module.\n\nThe file-versus-roster join arms are the other half of the same host: a skip in the derivation must still refuse. They execute inside run_rostered_row_join on the required parse path (witnesses lane). file_roster_join_tests are the off-path REDs for those arms; they are enumerated because test items are still hand Rust.\n\nWHY ADMITTED AGAINST THE v1 FREEZE: gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing admits by PURPOSE. Removing the silent-drop constructor from the failure-mode ledger is an instrument tax every self-host lane was paying (merge hotspot). No new language behavior, no escape hatch, no emitted public surface.\n\nTHE BASE SIDE OF THE DERIVED ROSTER (gunbc#10856, three production items and three test items). is_derived_roster_path, roster_root_prefix and roster_from_path_listing exist because a DERIVED artifact has no base side in a diff and must not be inherited from the head. the roster module has no committed file (it is contributed in memory on the read path), so it can never appear in `git diff --name-status`, and the baseline reconstruction -- carrying forward every head record the diff did not touch -- was therefore standing the HEAD`s generated roster up as the BASE`s. That made an ordinary row append read as a name resolving into a pool rather than an authored reference, because the roster`s two sides were the same bytes. They live HERE rather than beside their caller for the reason this module exists: roster_from_path_listing renders through render_roster, the same function head acquisition uses, so the roster`s bytes keep ONE authority whether the question is asked of a directory or of a base tree listing. They carry the same trigger as the rest of this population -- with declaration-value binding the derivation has no name-list at all, on either side, and these delete with the derivation.\n\nTHE SECOND LEDGER, NOT A SECOND MECHANISM (gunbc.rung_drop cutover). gunbc.rung_drop.roster was a hand-appended list, so a drop file nobody also listed there was absent from docs/design-rung-drops.md. The same fold now derives it: DerivedRowRoster is one table row per ledger (DERIVED_ROW_ROSTERS), and declares_row selects a sibling file only when it declares its own stem as a row of the ledger's type, because the rung-drop directory also holds helper modules (shared_capability, standing). That selector is a line-shape read and not the authority on what was declared; the parse join's DeclaredNotRostered reads the compiled population and refuses any RungDrop row it missed. The base side reads each listed row file at the base revision for the same reason. These carry the same trigger as the rest of the population.\n\nRe-derive this list with tools.seed_growth_change_population rather than maintaining a count.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "THE SUBJECT IS THESE DECLARATIONS, and they retire with declaration introspection sufficient to BIND a discovered data declaration as a typed value of its declared type — the same capability named by gunbc.guarantee_stall.roster_re_enumerates_its_own_rows_stall — at which point the host fold and the file-join arms DELETE because there is no authored or derived name-list to omit a row from. A differently named hand writer is not dissolution: it is this obligation under a new key. Registering roster.dag on gunbc.generated_artifact does not discharge this: that would restore heal/drift rewrite of a gitignored file. data_decl_type_facts already exists and does not discharge a trigger that names BINDING.",
  current_boundary: "v1_compiler.cli_run.derived_row_roster is reached from run_required_wave_admission (is_derived_roster_path, roster_root_prefix and roster_from_path_listing, the phase`s base side; namespace_baseline reads a committed base roster as source and synthesizes none beside it), from entry_source_from_index_or_disk (is_derived_roster_path, answering an entry that names a derived roster from the index), and through acquire_dir_files from every source-acquisition walk: collect_dag_files_result, collect_dag_files_tolerant (which now returns a located refusal for a roster it cannot derive instead of swallowing it), main.rs collect_dag_files, compiler_tests collect_dag_recursive, and run_dag_parse_sweep (the required-CI parse phase). Consumers of those walks receive AcquiredDag and read through it, so module indexing, import and reference discovery, entry lookup, for_each_parsed_module_binding, try_build_module_index, try_index_source_root_into_module_index, decl_facts_corpus_walk and decls_parse_only_from_disk see the same population as the parse sweep. Nothing writes under a source root. Its DERIVED_ROW_ROSTERS table covers gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster and gunbc.rung_drop.roster. join_row_files_to_roster_members is reached only from join_recurring_failure_mode_files_to_roster inside run_rostered_row_join. Legacy roster files left by older binaries are gunbc.repo_workspace SupersededAuthority rows, retired by gunbc.live_deploy.repository_convergence retire_superseded_workspace_files during deployed-tree convergence. Docs gate main agrees only DesignRungDropsArtifact."
}
